    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="0687" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/2392</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-15">March 15, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador<anchor n="35" xml:id="d705-f1"/> called at his request. He said
                    that health conditions in Syria were very bad and that his Government desired
                    that this Government request the cooperation of Great Britain to permit medical
                    products from the United States to be sent to Syria and Lebanon. I replied that
                    I would be glad to take this matter up with the British.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d705-f1" n="35" xml:id="d705-f1-content">
                <p>The French Ambassador, Gaston Henry-Haye.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
